  "question": {
    "text": "Consider three lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.&nbsp;If these lines form a triangle <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, then the sum of the squares of the tangent of all the interior angles of the triangle is",
